{"seq":15,"trial_id":"v03-opus-dev-2026-10/openclaw-opus-gbrain-told-company-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-01T10:15:58.205Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"1a39d10a8e9de74fb344e3b390b8d7e453240c80a0219c29960edc0f8c4ecc11","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all six of Moss's digests in the share. Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched it that evening and Thea confirmed the fix on 5 Oct. There was also an action item to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nThe other QFL mentions don't include a ticket number: the 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23 renewal check-in. Moss's two Central files mention #4409, #4412 and FR-882, but those belong to Central accounts, not QFL. The cheat sheet also warns not to mix QFL up with Quarendon Freightways (one \"r\"), which isn't a customer.\n\nSince #4419 is in an undated note, check that it's still current before it goes into the weekly notes.","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","ts":"1791987000.000124","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"}}
{"seq":16,"trial_id":"v03-opus-dev-2026-10/openclaw-opus-gbrain-told-company-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-01T10:16:04.165Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"b76f5201794cc9d6a380b2f0752ae8bed0685675f6fb2beaa0406ff6ecc6beec","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","text":"I replied in your DM thread. Moss's notes mention two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n- **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the fix on 5 Oct.\n- **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because gatehouse scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was sent up to tier-2 support to test the scanner firmware.\n\nThat note has no date, so check that #4419 is still current before it goes into the weekly notes.\n\nI went through all six of Moss's notes. Two others mention Quarrendon but give no ticket number: the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in. Moss's Central handoffs note lists #4409, #4412 and FR-882, but those are for a Central account, not Quarrendon. Moss's North cheat sheet also warns not to confuse Quarrendon Freight Lines with Quarendon Freightways (spelled with one \"r\"), which isn't a customer."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
